{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"misandrous-irritable-okapi","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nClients authoring epic plans can repeat volatile graph metadata by stating the current number of children, and can add a redundant acceptance criterion requiring every child to close. The packaged plan-review author guide at `src/rebar/_guides/writing-a-passing-plan.md` should steer them toward durable epic outcomes and decomposition instead; child closure is already enforced deterministically before parent completion as documented in `docs/llm-framework.md`.\n\n## Approach\nAdd concise container-specific guidance to the canonical packaged guide: do not state the child count in an epic description, and do not add a separate acceptance criterion for all children being closed/completed. Add a focused guide-content regression assertion. Rejected: changing plan-review or completion-verifier behavior, because the request concerns author guidance and the existing deterministic closure guard already supplies the invariant.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/_guides/writing-a-passing-plan.md`: clarify durable epic description and acceptance-criteria guidance.\n- `tests/unit/test_plan_review_explain.py`: assert the packaged plan guide retains both instructions.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `rebar explain plan` tells clients not to include the number of children in an epic description; verified by the packaged-guide unit test.\n- [ ] `rebar explain plan` tells clients an epic needs no separate acceptance criterion stating that all children are closed/completed; verified by the packaged-guide unit test.\n- [ ] Existing guide and repository checks pass from the worktree virtualenv.","id":"c2ec-6664-1571-490b","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["docs","plan-review"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Clarify epic child guidance in plan review author guide"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785199161369161001,"uuid":"df7c834a-00fe-4251-92b6-88dd7a41ec36"}